HEAD is now at 7400fd7 chore: claim T-006
=== launching claude for T-006 ===
T-006 is built and all three checks pass. The branch is pushed to `origin/agent/T-006` (commit `d745eb9`). I didn't merge, touch `main` or open a PR, since you asked only for a push. CLAUDE.md does say a PR is required for "done", so a PR still needs to be opened.

**Before merge: two edits outside the `Touches:` list, plus a module that is coded but not switched on**
- **Changed `apps/api/package.json` and `pnpm-lock.yaml`.** I added the `@pactlab/ai` workspace dependency (3 lines in the lockfile). Without it the documents code can't import the AI gateway.
- **Documents are not saved to a database yet.** Storage goes through an interface, and tests use an in-memory version. The tables for documents, pages, AI runs and document findings need a schema task, because `packages/db` isn't in my scope.
- **The documents module isn't mounted in the API.** That needs a change to `app.module.ts`, which is also out of scope. T-004 left its findings module in the same state.
- **No live connection to Claude.** The gateway sends requests through a pluggable "transport", and tests replay recorded responses with no network access. The real AWS Bedrock connection is left for T-007. Model IDs come from spec §11: Sonnet 5.5 is the default, and `anthropic.claude-opus-5-5` is my assumption from the spec's naming pattern.
- **Uploads accept text and Markdown only.** PDFs need an extraction library, which I didn't add. The API rejects them with 415.

**What's covered**
- **Uploads:** checks on file type, size and encoding; a virus-scan hook that refuses the upload if the scanner is down; storage under organization/deal-scoped keys; retention classes, with purge blocked under legal hold. The same file uploaded twice returns the existing document.
- **Q&A and contract extraction:** answers and extracted terms cite exact pages, and every quote must appear word-for-word on the cited page. Extraction only ever creates DRAFT findings.
- **Review:** only a deal lead or reviewer can accept or reject, and acceptance re-checks every citation against the current page text. HR-classified or AI-excluded documents never reach the model.
- **Acceptance criteria, tested:**
  - Every accepted finding has exact page citations and a named human reviewer. AI or unnamed reviewers are refused.
  - Citations to sources the model wasn't given, wrong-page quotes, paraphrases and quotes of injected instructions are all rejected.
  - Model output that tries to set a review status fails validation after one repair attempt, and text can't break out of the source markers.
- **Evals:** a small synthetic golden set runs in `pnpm test`. It requires 100% correct page citations and every probe blocked. It also fails if a prompt changes without re-recording the saved responses.
- **Web:** `/documents` shows the page on the left with cited quotes highlighted, and the review queue on the right with citation links and model/prompt labels. It shows the signed-out state for now, because web sign-in isn't wired yet.

**Files**
- `packages/ai/src/`: gateway, models, transport, context, citations, injection, grounding, hash, `prompts/{registry,document-qa,contract-extract,index}`, `evals/{golden,run,evals.test}`, plus tests (`gateway.test.ts`, `citations.test.ts`)
- `apps/api/src/documents/`: types, upload-policy, extraction, document-findings, repository, schemas, service, controller, module, testing doubles, `documents.unit.test.ts`, `documents.api.test.ts`
- `apps/web/app/(app)/documents/`: `page.tsx`, `_lib/view.ts`, `_lib/view.test.ts`
- `apps/api/package.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`

**Commands**
- `pnpm install`, then `pnpm --filter @pactlab/db generate`: both succeeded
- `pnpm lint`: exit 0, 15/15 tasks
- `pnpm typecheck`: exit 0, 15/15 tasks
- `pnpm test`: exit 0, 15/15 tasks (ai 35, api 54, web 9 tests; all other packages green)
- `prettier --write` on the new files only
- `git push -u origin agent/T-006`: succeeded

`tasks/active/T-006.md` hasn't been moved to `tasks/review`; I left that for the loop.

Separately: the Google Drive, Resend and Vercel connections need authorizing in their connector settings before they can be used. Nothing in this task depended on them.
